fact WorkItem(id: "WI-325", description: some(value: "Spec-op dispatch with abstract sort var and no covering requires-clause: report error instead of silently deferring. The typer's spec-op dispatch path at typing.rs:2109-2169 returns DispatchOutcome::NoCandidates silently when a body's spec-op call (e.g. eq(a, b) where a, b: T) hits an abstract sort variable in the substitution AND the enclosing operation's requires-chain doesn't cover the spec sort. The comment at 2130-2139 treats this as deliberate: 'Leaving the call as the spec op lets the runtime resolve it via its registered builtin or the spec's own derived rule.' This is correct for concrete sorts (Int.eq via host builtin, Eq.neq via derived rule) but UNSAFE for abstract sort vars without a requires-clause — the call site appears to type-check but will dispatch-fail at first runtime call. Example: List.member (added WI-324) calls eq(head, x) for abstract T but has no requires Eq[T]; typer accepts silently. Desired behavior: in req_insertion::run (or the typer's NoCandidates arm), distinguish concrete-sort NoCandidates (legitimate — leave the call alone) from abstract-sort-var NoCandidates with no covering requires (unsafe — report TypeError). The user then ADDS the explicit requires-clause to the operation signature; no auto-inference. This shifts the safety model from 'deferred to first call' to 'checked at body load'. Acceptance: 'operation foo(x: T) -> Bool = eq(x, x)' WITHOUT 'requires Eq[T]' fails to load with a diagnostic naming the missing requires (TypeError::MissingRequiresForSpecOp or equivalent). Adding 'requires Eq[T]' makes it load. cargo-test passes; existing stdlib that genuinely needs explicit requires (e.g. List.member after WI-324) is updated as part of the same patch. Driver: surfaced during WI-324 code-review (2026-05-28) — List.member's missing requires Eq[T] was a phantom finding because the NoCandidates path admits it silently; user feedback: 'we have insert_req pass, insert_req should insert or report' + 'we don't need inferred require clause'."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude-opus-4.7", at: "2026-05-29T05:58:58Z"))
